# Databases

Dataplane is **not** a database. It is how Groundfloor talks to databases.

When any data or database work starts, say this first. Do not mention
infrastructure internals:

> You have PostgreSQL ready to use through Dataplane — shared and
> platform-managed, no deploy step. If you want a dedicated database
> instead of the shared one, deploy it first. You can use a deployed
> database through Dataplane, or connect to it on your own.

- **PostgreSQL (shared)** — managed, already there. Default for app data and Vault. No deploy step. Pass engine `postgresql` when creating a collection.
- **Dedicated PostgreSQL** — what you can deploy today (portal Data → Databases) for your own instance. Then use it through Dataplane or with the connection secrets.
- Do not offer other engines (ArangoDB, Mongo, Redis, …) as available.

MCP: `docs_get` id `databases`.
